    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Gemma 4</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">Gemma 4 is Google DeepMind’s open-weight model family, described as built from Gemini 3 research and technology for intelligence-per-parameter. It is a separate stack from hosted Gemini Flash / Pro API SKUs. DeepMind’s Gemma 4 hub lists sizes including <strong>12B</strong>, <strong>26B</strong>, and <strong>31B</strong>, plus edge-oriented <strong>E4B</strong> and <strong>E2B</strong> variants in the performance table. Weights are offered via Hugging Face, Ollama, Kaggle, and LM Studio links on that hub. The Gemini API pricing page also lists Gemma 4 with free-tier access and paid tier marked not available.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />
    <p>DeepMind’s published table (IT Thinking variants) includes Arena AI (text, as of 2 Apr 2026) Elo 1452 for Gemma 4 31B, MMMLU 85.2%, MMMU Pro 76.9%, AIME 2026 89.2%, LiveCodeBench v6 80.0%, GPQA Diamond 84.3%, and τ2-bench Retail 86.4%. Capability framing on the hub: agentic workflows with native function calling, multimodal reasoning, support for 140 languages, fine-tuning, and local/edge deployment.</p>
    <p>Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index (secondary): Gemma 4 31B 19* on https://artificialanalysis.ai/leaderboards/models (fetched 22 Sep 2026). AA also lists other Gemma 4 sizes; those Index figures are on the same leaderboard if needed.</p>
    <p>This page is a short stub for the open-weight door. Full six-heading treatment is reserved for hosted Gemini Flash and Pro.</p>
